.TH LED 1 "2026-11-20" "1.0.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
led \- Larry's Editor, a terminal-based text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B led
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fI+line\fR] [\fIfile\fR[\fI:line\fR[\fI:col\fR]]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B led
is a terminal-based editor for C and C++ with unlimited undo/redo, auto-save/backups, syntax highlighting, and incremental rendering. Text lives in a subwindow; border only on full repaint.
Open at a compiler location with
.B led +142 file.c
or
.B led file.c:142:8
(1-based).
A name that already exists, colon and all, is opened as itself.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t
Test mode: run model/view/controller tests to stderr, exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix " dir"
Keep the config files in \fIdir\fR/led/, not ~/.config/led/.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B Arrows, Home/End (×2 top/bottom), PgUp/PgDn
Move and scroll.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Left / Ctrl+Right, Esc b / Esc f
Previous / next word. Ctrl+W deletes the previous word.
.TP
.B Ctrl+]
Jump to the matching parenthesis, bracket, or brace. Strings, comments, and C++ raw strings are skipped.
.TP
.B Ctrl+G
Go to a 1-based line, or line:col. Esc cancels.
.SS Editing
.TP
.B Printable, Enter, Backspace/Delete, Tab, Shift+Tab, Ctrl+Z/Y
Insert, newline, delete, tab, outdent, undo/redo.
Enter at the end of a line copies that line's indent, and adds one level after an opening brace or parenthesis.
.TP
.B Ctrl+K
Toggle a // comment on the current line.
.SS File
.TP
.B Ctrl+S / Ctrl+Q
Save / Quit. Save replaces the file by rename and keeps its mode.
Ctrl+Q on a modified buffer asks for a second Ctrl+Q.
.SS Selection
.TP
.B Ctrl+A / Ctrl+C / Ctrl+X / Ctrl+V
Select all / Copy / Cut / Paste (paste filtered).
After Ctrl+A, Copy, Cut, Backspace and Delete act on the whole buffer.
Without a selection, Copy and Cut take from the cursor to the end of the line.
.SS Search
.TP
.B Ctrl+/ / Ctrl+R
Search / Replace (regex, wraps to the top).
Ctrl+/ is byte 31, or the modified-key sequence the terminal sends for that chord
(\fCESC [27;5;47~\fR or \fCESC [47;5u\fR). The sequence is not inserted.
.SS Display
.TP
.B F2
Line numbers.
.TP
.B F3
Word wrap.
.TP
.B F4
Border on/off. On: the text is inset by one cell inside a box. Off: the text is full-width so xterm block-select copies only text. Paste filter strips \fC| │ ─ ┌┐└┘\fR. Config \fCshow_border\fR, env \fCLED_NO_BORDER=1\fR.
.SH WHAT WORKS
.IP \(bu 2
Data safety, undo/redo (one step per key press, cut, or paste), autosave.
A recovery file is written when the terminal closes.
A file that did not load whole is never written back.
.IP \(bu 2
Editing, selection, clipboard, regex search/replace, Unicode, incremental rendering (75x less output).
.IP \(bu 2
Syntax highlight for C and C++: reserved words, semicolons, and brackets coloured by nesting depth.
Strings, character literals and comments are left plain.
.IP \(bu 2
Subwindow border + paste-time border filter (replaces \fCtr -d\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
353 tests.
.SH WHAT FAILS
.IP \(bu 2
Whole-file in memory, no mmap; lines >10k truncated.
.IP \(bu 2
Errors not standardized, no per-buffer undo persistence.
Replace cannot be undone and clears the undo history.
.IP \(bu 2
Comments, strings and numbers have no colour of their own.
.IP \(bu 2
No fuzzing, still needs input sanitization, no OSC 52 clipboard.
.IP \(bu 2
xterm copy still sees screen cells — use F4 off.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Two files in \fC~/.config/led/\fR hold \fCkey=value\fR lines; \fC#\fR starts a comment.
\fCled.conf\fR has the general settings and \fCcolorization.conf\fR the colours and syntax words.
.B led
writes each on first run if it is missing, with every default shown as a comment. An existing file is never rewritten.
Either file may hold any key; \fCled.conf\fR is read last and wins.
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIdir\fR uses \fIdir\fR\fC/led/\fR in place of \fC~/.config/led/\fR.
List only the keys to change.
.SS Colors
The keys are
\fCnormal\fR, \fCselection\fR, \fCsemicolon\fR, \fCmeta_level1\fR to \fCmeta_level4\fR
(brackets by nesting depth) and \fCreserved_words\fR, each with \fC_fg\fR and \fC_bg\fR.
A value is one of the following, in any letter case.
.TP
.B BLACK RED GREEN YELLOW BLUE MAGENTA CYAN WHITE
The eight standard colors. These are the dark set.
.TP
.B BRIGHT_\fIname\fB, LIGHT_\fIname\fB
The bright variant of one of the eight, for example \fCLIGHT_BLUE\fR.
.B GRAY
is bright black.
.TP
.B 0 \fRto\fB 255
A color by number, for a terminal with extended colors.
.TP
.B DEFAULT
The terminal's own foreground or background.
.PP
The sixteen named colors and their numbers:
.PP
.nf
\fC0  BLACK      8  GRAY
1  RED        9  LIGHT_RED
2  GREEN     10  LIGHT_GREEN
3  YELLOW    11  LIGHT_YELLOW
4  BLUE      12  LIGHT_BLUE
5  MAGENTA   13  LIGHT_MAGENTA
6  CYAN      14  LIGHT_CYAN
7  WHITE     15  LIGHT_WHITE\fR
.fi
.PP
Defaults: text WHITE on BLACK, selection BLACK on WHITE,
semicolon and reserved words RED,
nesting levels 1 to 4 BLUE, CYAN, GREEN, YELLOW.
.PP
The bright variants are colors 8 to 15 on a terminal with 16 or more colors.
On a terminal with eight, a bright foreground is shown as the plain color in bold,
and a bright background as the plain color.
A number the terminal does not have is shown as white.
Give every \fC_bg\fR key the same value, or the background changes from word to word.
See
.BR curs_color (3X).
.PP
Example:
.PP
.nf
\fCmeta_level1_fg=LIGHT_BLUE
reserved_words_fg=LIGHT_RED
normal_bg=DEFAULT\fR
.fi
.SS Syntax
\fCsyntax_extensions\fR lists the file endings that are highlighted.
\fCreserved_words\fR lists the words colored as reserved.
\fCpaired_keywords\fR lists \fIopen\fR-\fIclose\fR word pairs colored by nesting depth.
A pair is used only when both of its words, or neither, are reserved words,
so the default \fCif-then\fR is ignored for C.
.SS Other keys
\fCshow_border\fR (F4), \fCshow_line_numbers\fR, \fCshow_key_meter\fR,
\fCtab_width\fR, \fCspaces_for_tab\fR,
\fCmax_file_size_mb\fR, \fCmemory_limit_mb\fR, \fCmax_line_length\fR.
Env \fCLED_NO_BORDER=1\fR.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/led/led.conf
.br
.I ~/.config/led/colorization.conf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curs_color (3X),
.BR vim (1),
.BR emacs (1),
.BR nano (1)
